{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LadderCoeffNormalisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderCoeffNormalisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Deriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.normalisedQuadCoeff_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.normalisedQuadCoeff_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCoeffNormalisation.lean#L144-L151","doc":"**At the committed `c₂ = −1`, the normalised coefficient is `−9/8`.**\n\nThe two numbers the collision was reported as a discrepancy between. They are\nthe same model, read at two normalisations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.normalisedQuadCoeff_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.normalisedQuadCoeff_eq","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCoeffNormalisation.lean#L130-L142","doc":"**`c̃₂ = c₂ − 1/8`** — the exact offset between the two readings.\n\nIndependent of `A`: the phase cancels in the normalisation, so the offset is a\nclean rational rather than an anchor-dependent quantity. This is what makes\n`c₂` and `c̃₂` two names for one model rather than a contradiction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.normalisedQuadCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.normalisedQuadCoeff","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCoeffNormalisation.lean#L124-L128","doc":"The normalised quadratic (Taylor) coefficient of the model: the second\nderivative at `0`, divided by `2!` and by the model's own value at `0`. This\nis the `c̃₂` of the naming ruling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.deriv_deriv_ladderModel_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.deriv_deriv_ladderModel_zero","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCoeffNormalisation.lean#L111-L122","doc":"**The model's second derivative at `0` is `cos A · (2c − 1/4)`.**\n\nThe `−1/4` is the cosine factor's own contribution and the `2c` is the\nexplicit factor's; they are separate terms, which is exactly why reading the\nsame model at two normalisations gives two different \"quadratic\ncoefficients\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.deriv_ladderModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.deriv_ladderModel","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCoeffNormalisation.lean#L104-L109","doc":"`deriv` of the model, as a function — needed to iterate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hasDerivAt_ladderModel'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hasDerivAt_ladderModel'","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCoeffNormalisation.lean#L90-L102","doc":"Second derivative of the model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hasDerivAt_ladderModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hasDerivAt_ladderModel","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCoeffNormalisation.lean#L81-L88","doc":"Product rule for the model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hasDerivAt_cosFactor'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hasDerivAt_cosFactor'","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCoeffNormalisation.lean#L70-L79","doc":"`d/dx sin(A − x/2)/2 = −cos(A − x/2)/4`. The two halvings compose to the\nquarter, which is where the eventual `1/8` comes from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hasDerivAt_cosFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hasDerivAt_cosFactor","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCoeffNormalisation.lean#L61-L68","doc":"`d/dx cos(A − x/2) = sin(A − x/2)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ladderModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ladderModel","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCoeffNormalisation.lean#L56-L59","doc":"The committed one-rung model: the cosine factor times the explicit\nquadratic factor `(1 + c x²)`. In the producer, `c = c₂ = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cosFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cosFactor","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCoeffNormalisation.lean#L52-L54","doc":"The ladder's cosine factor as a function of the ladder variable, with the\nphase `A` held fixed. In the producer this is `cos(α − u/2)` with `A = α`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}